  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 348 AM MDT Thu Jul 23 2026\n\nWhile isolated showers and thunderstorms will still impact the high \nterrain today, our weather pattern will trend drier and warmer as a \nridge of high pressure amplifies over the region. Storms today will \nbe capable of outflow winds up to 45 mph. We should see daytime \nhighs warm by several additional degrees today due to decreased \ncloud cover. Temperatures on Friday will be noticeably warmer as \nthey increase to well-above normal again in the mid- to upper-90s \nacross the low elevations and 80s in the mid-elevations and mountain \nvalleys. Daytime temperature will remain stable through the entirety \nof the forecast period. A shortwave on Saturday will bring increased \nchances for showers and thunderstorms in an otherwise dry-leaning \npattern. Winds will also increase on Saturday with many areas \nexpected to observe 30 to 40 mph gusts.",
